<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak FinMin 5-wk T-bill yield rises to 8.039 pct.</title>
<headline>Slovak FinMin 5-wk T-bill yield rises to 8.039 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average yield at the Slovak finance ministry five-week treasury bill auction hit 8.039 percent, up from 6.591 percent in the last auction of similar bills on May 22, the National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>					   Sept 11	 May 22</p>
<p> Bids (billion crowns)	     2.600	    2.640</p>
<p> Bids accepted			 1.650	    1.120</p>
<p> Minimum yield (pct)		 7.950	    5.920</p>
<p> Average yield (pct)		 8.039	    6.591</p>
<p> Maximum yield (pct)		 8.150	    6.740</p>
<p> Maturity date			 Oct 16	   June 26</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-210-3687</p>
</text>
